+# Deploy configs — COOP/COEP headers
+
+Every file here does the exact same thing, one per platform: sets
+
+```
+Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
+Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
+```
+
+That's it. It's a real browser security requirement for `SharedArrayBuffer`,
+which PSP's only available EmulatorJS core build needs — not something
+specific to this project. `loadGame("psp", ...)` throws a clear error if
+your page isn't cross-origin isolated, pointing you back here.
+
+If you're not using PSP, you don't need any of this.
+
+| Platform | File | How to use it |
+|---|---|---|
+| Cloudflare Pages | [`cloudflare-pages/_headers`](cloudflare-pages/_headers) | Copy to your build output root. Cloudflare Pages picks up a file literally named `_headers` automatically — no dashboard config. |
+| Netlify | [`netlify/netlify.toml`](netlify/netlify.toml) | Copy to your project root. (Netlify also supports the same `_headers` file syntax as Cloudflare Pages if you'd rather not use `netlify.toml` — pick one, not both.) |
+| nginx | [`nginx/coop-coep.conf`](nginx/coop-coep.conf) | `include` it inside your `server {}` (or `location {}`) block. |
+| Express | [`express/coop-coep-middleware.js`](express/coop-coep-middleware.js) | `app.use(coopCoepMiddleware)` — register it **before** `express.static`, so it runs on every response. |
+
+One caveat worth testing for yourself after deploying: `COEP: require-corp`
+requires every cross-origin resource on the page (EmulatorJS's `loader.js`
+and core/data files from `cdn.emulatorjs.org`, or your own self-hosted
+mirror) to either send `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy` itself or be fetched
+`crossorigin="anonymous"`. EmulatorJS's CDN has historically served the
+right CORS headers for its own assets — verify PSP specifically after you
+deploy, and self-host (see the main [README](../README.md#self-hosting-instead-of-the-public-cdn))
+if you ever hit a COEP-blocked resource.
